Restricted Optional Components
The optional world feature can use apple/ml-sharp and its model assets. The source
package includes Apple software and model license files in upstream distributions.
CE source releases and Docker images must not bundle Apple model weights.

FaceSwap Live (换脸直播)
The optional face-swap live feature ships a self-developed local sidecar engine
under services/faceswap (Elastic License 2.0). It uses only permissively-licensed
libraries (insightface MIT, onnxruntime MIT, opencv Apache-2.0, pyvirtualcam
MIT, fastapi/uvicorn MIT), installed at runtime into a SEPARATE venv under
<STATE_DIR>/faceswap/venv that is NOT part of this repository's dependency tree
(pyproject/uv.lock) and is NOT distributed in CE source or Docker images. The
upstream Deep-Live-Cam project is AGPL-3.0; its code is NOT linked, vendored, or
copied here — the main backend controls the sidecar only over 127.0.0.1 HTTP with
zero imports, so no copyleft obligation propagates into the Elastic-2.0 distribution.
Face-swap model weights (insightface inswapper/buffalo_l, GFPGAN, etc.) are
downloaded by the user at runtime, are not bundled, and carry non-commercial/research
licenses that are the user's own responsibility.

